# Pinned toolchain + source versions for the libgit2-WASM build.
#
# Both values below were checked against each project's own authoritative
# version source in the session that authored this build pipeline (not
# guessed, not carried over from training-data memory, which would be
# stale by definition):
#
#   LIBGIT2_REF  — confirmed via `GET api.github.com/repos/libgit2/libgit2/releases`:
#                  v1.9.6 is the current latest release (published
#                  2026-07-18, four days before this phase was authored),
#                  a maintenance release on the 1.9 branch (bugfixes only,
#                  see its release notes) — a sensible pin: recent, stable,
#                  not a moving target like a branch HEAD.
#
#   EMSDK_VERSION — confirmed via emsdk's own version manifest
#                  (raw.githubusercontent.com/emscripten-core/emsdk/main/
#                  emscripten-releases-tags.json), whose `aliases.latest`
#                  field is `"6.0.3"`, resolving to commit
#                  9074aa513b501925adb1361e208932ad32a29a5f in the
#                  emscripten-releases repo. `emsdk install <version>` /
#                  `emsdk activate <version>` accept this version string
#                  directly.
#
# Both pins were re-confirmed still current, then actually used to compile
# and link a real .wasm/.js pair (see BUILD.md) — this is no longer a
# theoretical pin, it's the exact version combination that built
# build/dist/tether-libgit2.{js,wasm}. Re-verify again before bumping either
# value, and re-run the tests/libgit2/ suite afterward.

LIBGIT2_REF=v1.9.6
EMSDK_VERSION=6.0.3
